    faq=[
        ("Which Scrum certification is most recognised?", "PSM I from Scrum.org and CSM from Scrum Alliance are the most widely recognised entry-level Scrum Master certifications. Scrum.org's published count shows over 778,000 PSM I holders as of 1 November 2026."),
        ("Which is harder, PSM I or CSM?", "Most people find PSM I harder: it has an 85% pass mark and no required course. The CSM test has a 74% pass mark and follows a 16-hour course that covers the material."),
        ("Can I get Scrum certified without taking a course?", "Yes. All Scrum.org certifications, including PSM I and PSPO I, can be earned by passing the online assessment without a course. Scrum Alliance certifications require a course; the SAFe Scrum Master exam can be bought as a proctored exam without the course."),
        ("Do Scrum certifications expire?", "Scrum.org certifications do not expire and have no renewal fee. Scrum Alliance certifications renew every two years with SEUs and a fee ($100 for CSM or CSPO). SAFe certifications renew annually."),
        ("How much does Scrum certification cost?", "PSM I and PSPO I cost US$200 per attempt. CSM and CSPO are included in a course fee set by the trainer; Scrum Alliance quotes $250 to $2,495 for CSM based on October 2023 prices. The SAFe Scrum Master proctored exam is $495."),
        ("How long does it take to get Scrum certified?", "A CSM or CSPO takes the course length, usually two or three days, plus the CSM test. For PSM I, most people new to Scrum need a few weeks of study; experienced practitioners may need only a few days."),
        ("What is the best Scrum certification for beginners?", "PSM I or CSM for aspiring Scrum Masters, and PSPO I or CSPO for aspiring Product Owners. None requires prior experience. Choose by how you prefer to learn and what employers in your market ask for."),
        ("Can I study for a Scrum certification for free?", "Yes. The Scrum Guide is free, and Scrum.org offers free open practice assessments. You only pay for the PSM I or PSPO I assessment itself."),
        ("Is there a Scrum certification for Developers?", "Yes. Scrum.org's Professional Scrum Developer (PSD) assessment covers Scrum and modern development practices, and Scrum Alliance offers Certified Scrum Developer (CSD) through its courses."),
        ("Is SAFe Scrum Master a worthwhile certification?", "It is useful if you work, or want to work, in an organisation that uses SAFe, because it covers how Scrum Teams operate on an Agile Release Train. Outside SAFe, PSM I or CSM are more widely recognised."),
        ("Is PMI-ACP a Scrum certification?", "Not exclusively. The PMI-ACP covers several Agile approaches, including Scrum, and requires Agile training and experience. Many people take PSM I or CSM first and the PMI-ACP later."),
        ("Can a PSM I holder take Scrum Alliance's advanced certification?", "Yes. Scrum Alliance accepts a Scrum.org PSM I or PSM II in place of the CSM as the prerequisite for the Advanced CSM, alongside 12 months of validated Scrum Master experience in the past five years."),
        ("What comes after an entry-level Scrum certification?", "Real experience first, then an advanced level such as PSM II or A-CSM, or a complementary credential such as PSK I or PSPO I. See our guide on [how to become a Scrum Master](/project-management/scrum/how-to-become-a-scrum-master/)."),
    ],
